  "body": "Action-required handoff to the canonical-implementor seat. PO authorized starting v0.1.1 work immediately. **The bundle:** (1) CA-011 — catdef_list_decisions tool returns 'GitHub API 401 listing decisions/' at both anonymous and elevated tiers; SAME root cause affects POST /mcp/admin/refresh-counter (verified during strategist dogfood test 2026-05-26 14:35). Both call into the same GitHub directory-listing API path. Single fix unblocks both surfaces. Strategist disposition notes (triaged via MCP): provision GITHUB_TOKEN env var on the Cloudflare Worker (lifts unauth rate-limit ceiling from 60/hr to 5000/hr; no special permissions needed beyond public read), OR pre-build a static decisions index at deploy time. (2) CA-012 — dynamic resource URI inconsistency: catdef://spec/decisions/CA-NNN works without .md but stable resources include .md; catdef://decisions/CA-NNN (no spec/ prefix) also fails. Two-phase fix: v0.1.1 accepts both URI forms with and without .md extension; v0.2 exposes resourceTemplates in catdef_describe per MCP-spec convention to close the discovery gap. Also document URI conventions in MCP_REFERENCE.md (maintainer task; cross-reference). (3) CA-013 Call 1 — sunset the createGitHubIssue invocation on the legacy POST /feedback handler. Per CA-008 privacy posture (private at submission; public via curation), submission method should not determine privacy state. Existing GitHub issues from past auto-created submissions stay as historical record; just stop creating new ones. The legacy handler continues to mint CA-NNN identifiers and land feedback in the queue. (4) CA-013 Call 2 — add .github/workflows/deploy.yml triggering on push to main, deploying via `wrangler deploy` with CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN from repo secrets. Standard pattern. Add a small DEPLOYING.md so the PO can rotate the token without spelunking through workflow YAML. **Bundle order (per CA-013 §Notes for the canonical-implementor seat):** CA-011 first (load-bearing; tool currently broken); CA-012 second (friction); CA-013 Call 1 third (feedback-handler edit, bundles with feedback-related work); CA-013 Call 2 separately if scheduling demands. **CA-NNN collision-risk acceptance:** PO authorized accepting the risk during the v0.1.1 fix window (option c). The MCP counter is currently at 12; next allocation = CA-013, which collides with the just-committed decisions/CA-013.md. No active feedback submissions expected during the fix window; the collision is recoverable post-fact if it materializes. Fix CA-011 first to unblock refresh-counter, then refresh-counter to sync past CA-013. **CA-013 Call 3 — seat bot identity ratification:** no action from this seat. The provisional `canonical-implementor@catdef.org` identity used on catdef-plugin commit e641be2 and catdef.org commit 5d3e453 is now ratified as canonical; future commits continue under the same identity without 'provisional' wording. Governance text update is a separate catdef-maintainer task. **Standing posture:** v0.1.1 bundle is the immediate canonical-implementor priority; v0.2 work (feedback_audit table, mechanical catdef_validate port, Durable Object for CA-NNN allocation) follows on this seat's clock. **Status reporting expected back:** memo to catdef-strategist when v0.1.1 ships, with verification curls confirming CA-011 + CA-012 are resolved and Call 1 + Call 2 are live. **Note on MCP queue access for this seat:** the catdef-strategist + catdef-maintainer seats have Director-issued elevated keys; the canonical-implementor seat does NOT yet have one. For v0.1.1 work you do NOT need elevated MCP access — CA-011 / CA-012 reproduction is anonymous-tier; CA-013 Calls 1+2 are code edits in the catdef.org repo. If you want to verify your own fix end-to-end post-deploy, ping the PO to mint an elevated key for this seat (or a standard key if elevated isn't needed). Not blocking; flagged for completeness.",

